---
export const title = 'Intents';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>intent</code> sets the meaning, with a matching icon, label and color role: <code>note</code> (neutral,
  the default), <code>info</code>, <code>success</code>, <code>warning</code> and <code>danger</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-alert intent='note' description='General guidance for a non-blocking context.'></wc-alert>

  <wc-alert intent='info' description='A neutral informational message for users.'></wc-alert>

  <wc-alert intent='success' description='Your settings were saved successfully.'></wc-alert>

  <wc-alert intent='warning' description='Check this value before continuing.'></wc-alert>

  <wc-alert intent='danger' description='We could not complete your request.'></wc-alert>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  <code>variant</code> for meaning (<code>variant='warning'</code>, <code>variant='error'</code>, ...) is
  deprecated and will be removed in 4.0: use <code>intent</code>, where <code>error</code> is
  <code>danger</code>. The old values still work and log a console warning.
</p>
